Lysis — Authors and Contributors
=================================

This file acknowledges the people who have contributed to Lysis. It is a
record of authorship and contribution, not a definitive statement of copyright
ownership; see LICENSE for the terms under which this software is distributed.

Note on copyright: the underlying mathematical model and algorithms are not
themselves subject to copyright; copyright attaches to the specific source code
expressing them. Several contributions were made in the course of work at the
University of Central Oklahoma, so the university may hold copyright in some or
all of this code. Ownership questions should be directed to UCO.


Originator of the Model
-----------------------

Dr. Brittany Bannish <bbannish@uco.edu> (https://github.com/bbannish)
    Originator of the fibrinolysis model, its algorithms, and the original
    Fortran implementation of the microscale and macroscale code on which this
    project is built.


Primary Author and Maintainer
------------------------------

Dr. Bradley Paynter <bpaynter@uco.edu> (https://github.com/bpaynter)
    Python package and processing pipeline, data structures and HDF5 I/O,
    command-line interface, C++ port of the macroscale code, modifications to
    the original Fortran, documentation, and ongoing maintenance.


Contributors
------------

Corey Beadle (https://github.com/researchercb)
    C++ and Fortran code contributions.

Eli Payton (https://github.com/Eli-Payton)
    Python utilities, data-specification work, HDF5 file building, and
    exploratory notebooks.

Tyler Pumphrey (https://github.com/wpumphrey)
    Continuous-integration (GitHub Actions) workflows, usage documentation,
    and scripts.

Austin Segrest (https://github.com/Austin9429)
    MATLAB code and usage documentation.

Mirochill (https://github.com/Mirochill)
    Geometry module contributions.


If you have contributed to Lysis and are not listed here, or any attribution
above is inaccurate, please open an issue or contact the maintainer.
